# ATJ-ERP Design System Guidelines

This document defines the design system rules for the ATJ-ERP project. All components must follow these guidelines for consistency, accessibility, and maintainability.

## 🎨 Color System

### Color Variables
Always use CSS variables defined in `globals.css`. Never use hardcoded colors.

**Primary Colors:**
- `bg-primary` / `text-primary-foreground` - Main brand color
- `bg-secondary` / `text-secondary-foreground` - Secondary actions
- `bg-accent` / `text-accent-foreground` - Accent/highlight color
- `bg-destructive` / `text-destructive` - Error/danger actions

**Neutral Colors:**
- `bg-background` / `text-foreground` - Main background/text
- `bg-card` / `text-card-foreground` - Card backgrounds
- `bg-muted` / `text-muted-foreground` - Muted/secondary text
- `border-border` - Border color
- `bg-input` - Input background

**Usage Rules:**
- ✅ Use semantic color names (primary, secondary, destructive)
- ❌ Never use hardcoded colors like `bg-blue-500` or `text-gray-600`
- ✅ Always pair background with appropriate foreground color
- ✅ Support dark mode via CSS variables (automatic)

## 📏 Spacing System

### Standard Spacing Scale
Use these Tailwind spacing values consistently:

- **Tight (4px)**: `gap-1`, `space-y-1`, `p-1`, `m-1`
- **Small (8px)**: `gap-2`, `space-y-2`, `p-2`, `m-2`
- **Medium (16px)**: `gap-4`, `space-y-4`, `p-4`, `m-4`
- **Large (24px)**: `gap-6`, `space-y-6`, `p-6`, `m-6`
- **XLarge (32px)**: `gap-8`, `space-y-8`, `p-8`, `m-8`

### Component-Specific Spacing

**Form Components:**
- Input padding: `px-3 py-2` (12px horizontal, 8px vertical)
- Form field spacing: `space-y-2` (8px between label and input)
- Form section spacing: `space-y-4` (16px between form fields)

**Layout Components:**
- Card padding: `p-6` (24px all around)
- Card content gap: `gap-6` (24px between sections)
- Dialog padding: `p-6` (24px all around)
- Container padding: `px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8` (responsive)

**Navigation:**
- Menu item spacing: `gap-2` or `space-x-2` (8px)
- Navigation container: `px-4` or `px-6` (responsive)

**Tables:**
- Cell padding: `px-4 py-3` (16px horizontal, 12px vertical)
- Row spacing: Automatic via border

## 🔲 Border Radius

### Standard Radius Values
Use CSS variables for border radius:

- **Small**: `rounded-sm` or `--radius-sm` (6px) - Small badges, chips
- **Medium**: `rounded-md` or `--radius-md` (8px) - Buttons, inputs, selects
- **Large**: `rounded-lg` or `--radius-lg` (10px) - Cards, dialogs, containers
- **XLarge**: `rounded-xl` or `--radius-xl` (14px) - Large containers
- **Full**: `rounded-full` - Badges, avatars, pills

### Component-Specific Radius
- Form inputs (input, select, textarea): `rounded-md`
- Buttons: `rounded-md` (default), `rounded-lg` (large)
- Cards: `rounded-lg`
- Dialogs: `rounded-lg`
- Badges: `rounded-full`
- Tables: No border radius (sharp corners)

## 🌑 Shadow Elevation

### Shadow Hierarchy
Use shadows to establish visual hierarchy:

- **Level 0 (Flat)**: No shadow - Backgrounds, containers
- **Level 1 (Raised)**: `shadow-xs` - Inputs, buttons, small cards
- **Level 2 (Floating)**: `shadow-sm` - Cards, panels
- **Level 3 (Modal)**: `shadow-lg` - Dialogs, modals, dropdowns
- **Level 4 (Overlay)**: `shadow-xl` - Tooltips, popovers (if needed)

### Component-Specific Shadows
- Form inputs: `shadow-xs`
- Buttons: No shadow (default), `shadow-xs` (outline variant)
- Cards: `shadow-sm`
- Dialogs: `shadow-lg`
- Tables: No shadow (contained in card)

## 📐 Component Heights

### Standard Heights
Maintain consistent heights for form controls:

- **Small**: `h-8` (32px) - Small buttons, compact inputs
- **Default**: `h-9` (36px) - Standard buttons, inputs, selects
- **Large**: `h-10` (40px) - Large buttons, table headers
- **Textarea**: `min-h-16` (64px minimum, flexible)

### Height Rules
- ✅ All form inputs (input, select) must be `h-9`
- ✅ Buttons match input height (`h-9` default)
- ✅ Textarea uses `min-h-16` (flexible height)
- ✅ Table headers use `h-10` for emphasis

## ✍️ Typography

### Font Size Scale
Use consistent font sizes:

- **XS**: `text-xs` (12px) - Badges, labels, captions
- **SM**: `text-sm` (14px) - Body text, descriptions, table cells
- **Base**: `text-base` (16px) - Default body, form inputs
- **LG**: `text-lg` (18px) - Section titles, card titles
- **XL**: `text-xl` (20px) - Page titles
- **2XL+**: `text-2xl`, `text-3xl` - Hero text, large headings

### Font Weight
- **Normal**: `font-normal` (400) - Body text
- **Medium**: `font-medium` (500) - Labels, buttons
- **Semibold**: `font-semibold` (600) - Titles, headings
- **Bold**: `font-bold` (700) - Emphasis, strong headings

### Component-Specific Typography
- Form labels: `text-sm font-medium`
- Form inputs: `text-base md:text-sm`
- Buttons: `text-sm font-medium`
- Card titles: `text-lg font-semibold` (or inherit from parent)
- Dialog titles: `text-lg font-semibold`
- Table headers: `text-sm font-medium`
- Table cells: `text-sm`

## 🎯 Focus States

### Standard Focus Pattern
All interactive elements must have consistent focus states:

```tsx
className="focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px]"
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ Use `focus-visible:` (not `focus:`) for keyboard navigation
- ✅ Border color: `border-ring`
- ✅ Ring color: `ring-ring/50` (50% opacity)
- ✅ Ring width: `ring-[3px]` (3px)
- ✅ Always include `outline-none` to remove default outline

## ⚠️ Error States

### Standard Error Pattern
All form inputs must support error states:

```tsx
className="aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive"
```

**Rules:**
- ✅ Use `aria-invalid` attribute for error state
- ✅ Error border: `border-destructive`
- ✅ Error ring: `ring-destructive/20` (light), `ring-destructive/40` (dark)
- ✅ Always pair with error message using `aria-describedby`

## ♿ Accessibility Requirements

### Required ARIA Attributes
- **Labels**: Always use `<label>` with `htmlFor` or `aria-label`
- **Errors**: Use `aria-invalid="true"` and `aria-describedby` for error messages
- **Required fields**: Use `aria-required="true"` or visual indicator
- **Disabled**: Use `disabled` attribute (not just styling)
- **Focus**: Ensure all interactive elements are keyboard accessible

### Keyboard Navigation
- ✅ All interactive elements must be focusable
- ✅ Use `tabIndex` only when necessary (avoid positive values)
- ✅ Provide visible focus indicators
- ✅ Support Enter/Space for button activation
- ✅ Support Escape to close modals/dialogs

## 🎨 Component Patterns

### Form Components Pattern
```tsx
// Standard form field structure
<div className="space-y-2">
  <label className="text-sm font-medium">
    Label Text
    {required && <span className="text-destructive ml-1">*</span>}
  </label>
  {description && (
    <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{description}</p>
  )}
  <Input
    aria-invalid={error ? "true" : "false"}
    aria-describedby={error ? `${id}-error` : undefined}
    className={error && "border-destructive"}
  />
  {error && (
    <p id={`${id}-error`} className="text-sm text-destructive" role="alert">
      {error}
    </p>
  )}
</div>
```

### Card Pattern
```tsx
<Card className="rounded-lg shadow-sm">
  <CardHeader className="px-6">
    <CardTitle className="text-lg font-semibold">Title</CardTitle>
    <CardDescription className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
      Description
    </CardDescription>
  </CardHeader>
  <CardContent className="px-6">
    {/* Content */}
  </CardContent>
</Card>
```

### Dialog Pattern
```tsx
<Dialog open={isOpen} onOpenChange={setIsOpen}>
  <DialogContent className="rounded-lg shadow-lg p-6">
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle className="text-lg font-semibold">Title</DialogTitle>
      <DialogDescription className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        Description
      </DialogDescription>
    </DialogHeader>
    {/* Content */}
    <DialogFooter className="gap-2">
      {/* Actions */}
    </DialogFooter>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

## 🔄 Transition & Animation

### Standard Transitions
Use consistent transitions for interactive elements:

- **Colors**: `transition-colors` - For color changes (hover, focus)
- **Shadows**: `transition-shadow` - For shadow changes
- **All**: `transition-all` - For multiple property changes (buttons)
- **Duration**: Default Tailwind (150ms) - No custom durations needed

### Animation Rules
- ✅ Use `transition-*` classes for smooth state changes
- ✅ Avoid custom animations unless necessary
- ✅ Keep animations subtle and purposeful
- ❌ Don't animate layout properties (causes jank)

## 📱 Responsive Design

### Breakpoint Strategy
Use Tailwind's default breakpoints:

- **sm**: 640px - Small tablets, large phones
- **md**: 768px - Tablets
- **lg**: 1024px - Small laptops
- **xl**: 1280px - Desktops
- **2xl**: 1536px - Large desktops

### Responsive Patterns
- Container padding: `px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8`
- Grid columns: `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`
- Text sizes: `text-base md:text-sm` (mobile-first)
- Spacing: `gap-2 md:gap-4 lg:gap-6`

## ✅ Component Checklist

When creating or modifying components, ensure:

- [ ] Uses CSS variables for colors (no hardcoded colors)
- [ ] Follows spacing scale (gap-2, gap-4, gap-6, etc.)
- [ ] Uses correct border radius for component type
- [ ] Has appropriate shadow elevation
- [ ] Includes focus states (focus-visible pattern)
- [ ] Supports error states (aria-invalid pattern)
- [ ] Has proper accessibility attributes
- [ ] Uses consistent typography scale
- [ ] Includes transitions for interactive elements
- [ ] Is responsive (mobile-first approach)
- [ ] Matches height standards (h-9 for form controls)
- [ ] Uses consistent padding patterns

## 🚫 Anti-Patterns (Don't Do This)

- ❌ Don't use hardcoded colors (`bg-blue-500`, `text-gray-600`)
- ❌ Don't mix spacing scales (`gap-3`, `gap-5` - use 2, 4, 6, 8)
- ❌ Don't use custom border radius values (use scale)
- ❌ Don't skip focus states on interactive elements
- ❌ Don't forget error state handling in forms
- ❌ Don't use inconsistent heights for form controls
- ❌ Don't mix shadow values arbitrarily
- ❌ Don't forget responsive design
- ❌ Don't skip accessibility attributes

